│[39m                                                                                                                      [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m With its permission option at full-access, dimcode may start other agent CLIs it finds on your PATH, such as claude, [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m codex and cursor, as subagents of its own, with their approvals bypassed and on your own accounts. At                [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m workspace-write it asks you first, and once you allow it, the same holds. Nothing those agents do reaches chord's    [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m permission box.                                                                                                      [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m                                                                                                                      [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m To turn a CLI off, set externalAgents.<type>.enabled to false in ~/.dimcode/v2/config.json (claude-code, codex,      [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m cursor, …), or use /external-agents in dimcode's own TUI. Or keep the permission option at read-only in /config,     [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m where dimcode refuses its agent tool.                                                                                [38;2;177;185;249m│
│[39m                                                                                                                      [38;2;177;185;249m│
